The VeeR EH2 testbench ties the JTAG reset inactive and the JTAG clock low, so
no event ever resets the tap. Its registers keep their default initial value,
which is x for a 4-state variable (IEEE 1800-2023 6.8, Table 6-7), and that x
reaches the debug module's write enable and then the core's reset. Tie the
reset low, as the EH1 and EL2 testbenches do.

Reported as https://github.com/verilator/rtlmeter/issues/52

diff --git a/designs/VeeR-EH2/src/tb_top.sv b/designs/VeeR-EH2/src/tb_top.sv
